From c6f6f02c6260579ce53ccfc1b3af89fab0ae20e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a fresh pin on a live quota wall
 reroutes in class instead of waiting the wall out

Review 5871917933 on #1320 (kanban-dd62aef001): the new pre-claim pinned_quota_wall hold stopped every
fresh pinned card on a live-pool wall before its first run. pinned_route rule 1 needs a wall from one of
the card's own runs, which a held card never gets, so a non-mandatory pin on a far wall with a free
class peer waited the whole wall out (the M4 56 h case the reroute was built for).

- kanban_pin_reroute.fresh_live_wall: a card with no run before its current one, whose concrete pin's
  live pool is quota-walled right now, counts that wall as rule 1 evidence (the same evidence its worker
  would exit 75 on). resolve_dispatch_tier passes it, so preview and admission reroute the first run.
- own_walls also reads earlier model_reroute events: a fresh card's reroute has no quota episode, and
  its next run must not go back into the wall it knows. record() names the live reset in the comment.
- kanban_dispatch_skip.pinned_quota_hold holds only when pinned_route would not reroute (mandatory pin,
  wall under pin_quota_reroute_min_hours, no eligible peer); an unreadable policy still holds.
- kanban_diagnostics: a current pinned_quota_wall skip with a future until is a deliberate hold
  (held_in_ready warning, with hold_until), not stranded_in_ready (critical after 3 h).
- record() dedupes pinned_quota_wall on until too, so a moved reset reaches the notice;
  per_profile_capped counts as an ordering skip (priority advice kept).

Proof: new tests test_fresh_pin_on_a_far_live_wall_reroutes_on_its_first_run (the reviewer's repro
shape: tick 1 spawns the peer, no dispatch_skipped, second run still on the peer, back on the pin after
the reset), test_fresh_pin_with_no_reroute_is_held_on_its_live_wall[mandatory|near_wall|no_peer]
(one skip, held_in_ready warning), plus dedupe/ordering tests. 9/9 mutants of the new conditions killed.
